    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T14:55:23Z",
    "body": "@shannonbooth is working on improving ongoing navigation handling in #12942. From a quick look, this seems compatible with that work: it lets the caller supply navigationId, while leaving its subsequent handling unchanged. @shannonbooth, does that match your understanding?\r\n\r\nCurrently there are no protections against collisions from [#dfn-generate-a-random-uuid](https://w3c.github.io/webcrypto/#dfn-generate-a-random-uuid), but allowing it to be passed could make us more exposed here, at least if it's implemented verbatim in an engine. Is there a way for us to protect against that?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
